    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SITE FOR SALE\r\nCIRCA 1.01 ACRES\r\nKNOCKLISCRANE, MILTOWN MALBAY, CO. CLARE.\r\n\r\nFOR SALE SUBJECT TO PLANNING PERMISSION\r\nCONTAINED IN FOLIO CE23086\r\n\r\nVIEWINGS STRICTLY BY ADVANCE APPOINTMENT WITH SOLE AGENT STREETS AHEAD PROPERTIES\r\nPROPERTY LICENCE NO 003178\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nStreets Ahead Properties are delighted to bring to the market this site circa 0.41 Hectares 1.01 acres, contained in Folio CE23086 subject to planning with circa 80 meters of road frontage on the R460 just off the R474 circa 2.7km from Miltown Malbay.  \r\n\r\nAn exceptional opportunity to acquire a well-located site in the heart of West Clare, just four minutes from the vibrant town of Miltown Malbay. Enjoy the perfect balance of peaceful countryside living while remaining within easy reach of local amenities, schools, cafés, and traditional music venues. Ideally positioned along the Wild Atlantic Way, the property is only a short drive from Spanish Point, White Strand, the Cliffs of Moher, and the spectacular Burren, making it an ideal location for a family home or coastal retreat.\r\n\r\nLocated on the R460. The property is located beside Eircode V95 CF70, *for directional purposes only*.   \r\n\r\nApproximately a 7-minute drive to the White Strand beach, approximately a 7-minute drive from Spanish Point beach and golf club and roughly an 8 minute drive to Seafield beach at Quilty. Spanish Point is a small seaside village in County Clare along the Wild Atlantic Way. It is known for its sandy beach, ocean views, and connection to the Spanish Armada, making it a peaceful spot for visitors.\r\n\r\nLahinch is easily accessible in approximately 16 minutes from the property, famous for its sandy beach, Promenade walk and 18-hole Championship golf course which the Irish Open was held 2019. There is also a newly refurbished Leisure Centre just recently reopened to the public and includes state-of-the-art gym and swimming pool.\r\n\r\nTrump International Golf Links & Hotel Doonbeg Ireland is only a 16-minute drive and is a luxury seaside golf resort in County Clare, set along the Atlantic coast. Originally opened in 2002 and later acquired by the Trump Organization, it features a renowned links-style course, upscale accommodation, and scenic ocean views, making it a popular destination for golfers visiting Ireland.\r\n\r\nMiltown Malbay is a Market town on Ireland’s west coast, known for its strong tradition of Irish music and welcoming community spirit. Situated along the Wild Atlantic Way, it is just inland from the seaside of Spanish Point, with its beautiful beaches and Atlantic views nearby. The town is internationally famous for the Willie Clancy Summer School, a major annual festival celebrating traditional music, song and dance. With its local pubs hosting regular music sessions. It has shops, pubs, restaurants and local services."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "All facilities close by.\r\n4 minutes to Miltown Malbay town.\r\nPivotal to the White Strand, Spanish Point beach and golf club, Seafield beach Quilty and Lahinch Beach, promenade and 18-hole championship golf club.\r\n80m of road frontage.\r\nConvenient to local schools, shops, cafés, pubs, and everyday amenities.\r\nGood road access to Ennistymon, Lahinch, Ennis, and Shannon Airport.\r\nIdeal location for a family home or holiday home.\r\nShort drive to the Cliffs of Moher, The Burren, and other Wild Atlantic Way attractions."
      }
    ],
